index 00000000..c416e01c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/channels/webhook/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,150 @@
+# 🔗 Webhook Channel
+
+PicoClaw can talk to any service that can send a signed HTTP request and receive one back. The service POSTs a message to PicoClaw; PicoClaw hands it to the agent and POSTs every reply to a URL of your choosing.
+
+## 🚀 Quick Start
+
+**1. Add the channel to `~/.picoclaw/config.json`:**
+
+```json
+{
+  "channel_list": {
+    "webhook": {
+      "enabled": true,
+      "type": "webhook",
+      "settings": {
+        "send_url": "http://localhost:9000/reply"
+      }
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+**2. Put the shared secret in `~/.picoclaw/.security.yml`:**
+
+```yaml
+channel_list:
+  webhook:
+    settings:
+      secret: your_shared_secret
+```
+
+**3. Start the gateway:**
+
+```bash
+picoclaw gateway
+```
+
+**4. Send a signed message:**
+
+```bash
+BODY='{"sender":"alice","content":"What is the CPU usage?","thread_id":"job-1"}'
+SIG=$(printf '%s' "$BODY" | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac "your_shared_secret" -hex | sed 's/^.* //')
+curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:18790/webhook/webhook \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -H "X-Webhook-Signature: sha256=$SIG" \
+  -d "$BODY"
+```
+
+The reply arrives as a POST to `send_url`.
+
+---
+
+## 📨 Inbound Request
+
+PicoClaw receives messages on the shared Gateway HTTP server (listening on `127.0.0.1:18790` by default), at the channel's `path`.
+
+```json
+{ "sender": "alice", "content": "your message here", "thread_id": "job-1" }
+```
+
+| Field | Required | Description |
+|-------|----------|-------------|
+| `content` | Yes | Message text. Must not be empty |
+| `thread_id` | No | Conversation identifier, used as the chat ID. Replies carry it back. Falls back to `sender` when empty |
+| `sender` | No | Sender identifier, matched against `allow_from` |
+
+The request must carry the header `X-Webhook-Signature: sha256=<hex>`, where `<hex>` is the HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body, keyed with `secret`.
+
+| Status | Meaning |
+|--------|---------|
+| `202` | The message was handed to the agent |
+| `400` | Malformed JSON, empty `content`, or neither `thread_id` nor `sender` given |
+| `401` | Missing or wrong signature |
+| `403` | The sender is not in `allow_from` |
+| `413` | Body larger than 1 MiB |
+| `503` | The channel is not running, or the message could not be handed to the agent |
+
+Any status other than `202` means the message was not delivered.
+
+---
+
+## 📤 Reply Request
+
+Every agent reply is POSTed to `send_url` with `Content-Type: application/json`:
+
+```json
+{ "content": "reply text", "thread_id": "job-1", "recipient": "job-1" }
+```
+
+`thread_id` and `recipient` both hold the chat ID of the request being answered. Tool-feedback progress messages are not sent.
+
+The receiver should answer `2xx`. Failures are classified like in other channels: `404` and other `4xx` are permanent, `429` and `5xx` (and network errors) are temporary and retried by the channel manager.
+
+---
+
+## ⚙️ Configuration
+
+| Field | Location | Required | Default | Description |
+|-------|----------|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `secret` | `.security.yml` | Yes | — | Shared secret for the request signature |
+| `send_url` | `settings` | Yes | — | URL that receives the replies |
+| `path` | `settings` | No | `/webhook/<channel name>` | Path to mount on the Gateway HTTP server |
+| `allow_from` | channel | No | all senders | Allowed `sender` values |
+
+The channel is not started until both `secret` and `send_url` are set.
+
+### Several instances
+
+Each entry in `channel_list` with `"type": "webhook"` is an independent channel with its own path, secret and send URL:
+
+```json
+{
+  "channel_list": {
+    "alerts": {
+      "enabled": true,
+      "type": "webhook",
+      "settings": {
+        "path": "/hooks/alerts",
+        "send_url": "http://localhost:9001/reply"
+      }
+    },
+    "helpdesk": {
+      "enabled": true,
+      "type": "webhook",
+      "settings": {
+        "send_url": "http://localhost:9002/reply"
+      }
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+```yaml
+channel_list:
+  alerts:
+    settings:
+      secret: alerts_secret
+  helpdesk:
+    settings:
+      secret: helpdesk_secret
+```
+
+Here `alerts` listens on `/hooks/alerts` and `helpdesk` on the default `/webhook/helpdesk`.
+
+---
+
+## ⚠️ Notes
+
+- **No media, typing indicator, placeholder or reactions**: the channel carries text only.
+- **HTTPS**: PicoClaw serves plain HTTP; put a reverse proxy in front of the Gateway if the sender is not on the same host.
